<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">22032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Twenty-three days of US-Israeli strikes have damaged eighty-one thousand homes across Iran, along with hospitals, schools, and ambulances.</s> <s>Iran's Red Crescent has called the campaign a violation of international humanitarian law and demanded an emergency international response.</s> <s>No ceasefire is in sight... and President Trump's forty-eight-hour ultimatum on the Strait of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="hɔːrˈmuːz">Hormuz</phoneme> has only deepened the crisis.</s>
</prosody>
<break time="900ms"/>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A drone struck <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɛl dɑːˈeɪn">el-Daein</phoneme> Hospital on <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="iːd">Eid</phoneme>, killing sixty-four people in Sudan.</s> <s>The <sub alias="World Health Organization">WHO</sub> has documented over two thousand deaths in two hundred and thirteen attacks on healthcare facilities since the civil war began in April twenty-twenty-three — what the UN calls the world's largest humanitarian crisis.</s> <s>The hospital can no longer function, and no one has claimed the strike.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israel's defense minister has ordered Lebanese border villages leveled — his words: "like Gaza" — to prevent one million displaced people from ever returning.</s> <s>The plan includes destroying <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kæsˈmiː.jə">Qasmiyeh</phoneme> Bridge near <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="tɔːr">Tyre</phoneme>, cutting the city off from the rest of the country.</s> <s>What Israel calls a buffer zone, Lebanon's government calls the permanent erasure of its southern border communities.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Biometric voting devices in Congo-Brazzaville came pre-loaded with results, handing President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="sæˈsuː ŋˈɡɛ.soʊ">Sassou-Nguesso</phoneme> ninety-four point eight percent of the vote.</s> <s>He's held power for forty of the last forty-seven years, and the devices he sold as democratic infrastructure were themselves the instruments of fraud.</s> <s>Civil society groups have filed a legal challenge, but overturning an election under a four-decade ruler has no precedent in the country.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Uganda's main opposition leader <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈboʊ.bi waɪn">Bobi Wine</phoneme> has fled the country, surfacing at the US Capitol.</s> <s>He lost the twenty-twenty-one presidential race to <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="muːˈsɛv.ən.i">Museveni</phoneme>, who's held power since nineteen eighty-six — making Uganda's most prominent opposition voice now a voice in exile.</s> <s>Wine says he'll meet American officials this week to press for his safe return.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israeli settlers shot six Palestinians dead in the West Bank in March alone, operating with de facto state protection under military occupation.</s> <s>Thirteen governments have demanded prosecutions that Israeli authorities won't carry out, while settler militias continue driving families from their land.</s> <s>European capitals have begun labeling this violence as terrorism — a word they rarely apply to the actions of their allies.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Cuba suffered its second national blackout in a week, and it was Puerto Rican activists — not any government — who flew medicine to Havana's hospitals.</s> <s>Washington offered diesel fuel, but only on condition of political concessions that Havana rejected.</s> <s>The US blockade restricts the medical supplies Cuba desperately needs, leaving the island caught between sovereignty and darkness.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India jailed thirty-three Bangladeshis, including children, for crossing the border.</s> <s>Justice and Care, a Bangladeshi rights organization, says the group were trafficking victims transported by paid brokers — not migrants who chose to cross.</s> <s>The networks that moved them remain active, and no brokers have been arrested.</s>
</p>
<break time="900ms"/>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's fuel supply is secured only through April, and Finance Minister <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈɔː.rəŋ.zɛb">Aurangzeb</phoneme> says the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="hɔːrˈmuːz">Hormuz</phoneme> crisis may last months.</s> <s>The government spent sixty-nine billion rupees on blanket fuel subsidies in March alone — a pace it can't sustain — and must now decide who gets cut off.</s> <s>Targeting criteria haven't been announced, and April's supply window is closing fast.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Indonesian President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="prɑːˈboʊ.woʊ suːbiˈɑːn.toʊ">Prabowo Subianto</phoneme> is targeting eight percent growth — a rate the country hasn't hit since the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="suːˈhɑːr.toʊ">Suharto</phoneme> era.</s> <s>His plan rests on thirty thousand school kitchens, eighty thousand village cooperatives, and one million new homes, but the government's own first-quarter forecast is five point five percent.</s> <s>The gap between ambition and arithmetic is a question <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="prɑːˈboʊ.woʊ">Prabowo</phoneme> hasn't answered.</s>
</p>
<break time="900ms"/>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Missiles have struck both <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="dɪˈmoʊ.nə">Dimona</phoneme> and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="næˈtænz">Natanz</phoneme> — two nuclear facilities on opposite sides of the Iran conflict.</s> <s>The <sub alias="International Atomic Energy Agency">IAEA</sub> detected no abnormal radiation, but <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="næˈtænz">Natanz</phoneme> holds enriched uranium stockpiles that would contaminate the entire region if dispersed.</s> <s><sub alias="World Health Organization">WHO</sub> Director-General <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈtɛd.roʊs ɑːdəˈnoʊm ɡɛbrɛˈjeɪ.sus">Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus</phoneme> has warned the conflict is edging toward a radiological disaster no health system can manage.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Medicare's own chief has called TrumpRx narrow, undercutting the president's drug-pricing promises.</s> <s>The program covers only cash-paying uninsured patients, leaving two hundred million insured Americans completely unaffected.</s> <s>Unless Congress legislates something broader, the vast majority won't see a penny of relief.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Boston Dynamics' Atlas still can't reliably grasp a small object — a problem that's humbled every humanoid robot ever built.</s> <s>The human hand's twenty-seven degrees of freedom require tactile feedback loops that current sensors simply can't replicate.</s> <s>Researchers say the breakthrough won't come from scaling existing designs... it'll require entirely new sensor technology.</s>
</p>
<break time="900ms"/>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>China's <sub alias="A S N three oh one">ASN-301</sub> drone is engineered to hunt and destroy radar systems, tracing its lineage to Israeli anti-radiation drone technology.</s> <s>Both the <sub alias="A S N three oh one">ASN-301</sub> and Iran's <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʃɑːˈhɛd">Shahed</phoneme> descend from the same Israeli <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈhɑːr.pi">Harpy</phoneme> design, but China optimized for precision where Iran optimized for mass production.</s> <s>Any nation relying on radar-guided air defenses now faces a weapon designed specifically to blind them.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A three-hundred-and-ninety-seven-billion-parameter AI model now runs on a consumer laptop.</s> <s>Mixture-of-experts architecture activates only four of five hundred and twelve expert networks per token, slashing the memory needed to run what was once a data-center-only model.</s> <s>Once downloaded, it can't be censored, updated, or remotely revoked — a line that, once crossed, doesn't uncross.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>